.TH THEME 6
.SH NAME
theme \- colors for rio, acme, menus and libcontrol programs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B $home/lib/theme
.br
.B /lib/theme
.SH DESCRIPTION
A theme names colors.
Programs read the first of
.B $home/lib/theme
and
.B /lib/theme
that exists, once, when they start;
a name the theme does not give keeps the program's own color,
so with no theme everything looks as it always has.
.PP
Each line is a name, then its colors, separated by blanks:
.IP
.EX
back	ffffff
tag	fg=000000 bg=eaffff
keyword	fg=0000aa
.EE
.PP
A color is six hexadecimal digits,
.IR rrggbb ,
with or without a leading
.LR # .
A bare color is the name's one color;
.BI fg= color
and
.BI bg= color
give text and background.
A name starts with a letter; a line that starts with
.L #
is a comment, and words a program does not know are ignored.
A later line for a name replaces an earlier one.
This is the format of 9front's rio themes, so their files serve as they are.
.PP
.IR Acme 's
per-window
.B style
file (see
.IR acme (4))
has the same lines, followed by runs:
.IP
.EX
keyword	fg=aa0000
0 6 keyword
12 20 comment
.EE
.PP
A run is a line of three fields: its start and length in runes, and a name.
A run whose name the window has not given takes the theme's colors,
so a program that marks text names roles and the theme chooses how they look.
For these a bare color is the text's.
.SS Names
.TP
.I rio
.BR back ,
.BR text ,
.BR high ,
.BR htext
and
.B border
for the windows' text,
.B ltext
for the text of windows other than the current one;
.B title
and
.B ltitle
for the current window's border and the others',
.BR hold ,
.B lhold
and
.B palehold
for those in hold mode,
.B size
for the outline as a window is swept,
.B rioback
for the background, and
.B wallpaper
for the picture on it, whose black becomes its
.B bg=
and white its
.BR fg= .
.TP
menus
.BR menuback ,
.BR menuhigh ,
.BR menubord ,
.B menutext
and
.BR menuhtext ,
for
.IR menuhit (2)
in every program.
.TP
.I acme
.B tag
and
.B body
for text and background,
.B tagsel
and
.B bodysel
for selections,
.B tagborder
and
.BR bodyborder ;
.B modbutton
and
.B colbutton
for the boxes at the left of tags,
.B but2
and
.B but3
for text swept with buttons 2 and 3,
.B colback
for space no window covers, and
.B colrule
for the lines between columns and windows.
For
.BR tag ,
.BR tagsel ,
.B body
and
.BR bodysel ,
a bare color is the background.
.TP
.I page
.B back
around the image, as
.IR page (1)
says.
.TP
style files
Acme's
.B style
files and
.IR astyles (4)'s
layers name roles, such as
.BR keyword ,
.B comment
and
.BR string ,
which the theme colors.
.B /lib/theme
gives those the system's programs use;
.IR alsp (4)
marks diagnostics
.BR error ,
.BR warning ,
.B info
and
.BR hint .
.TP
.IR control (2)
.BR back ,
.BR text ,
.BR border ,
.BR high ,
.BR pale ,
.B entry
and
.BR ok ,
which controls take when not told otherwise, and which programs such as
.I auth/fgui
(see
.IR factotum (4))
name.
.TP
.IR sketch (1)
.B back
and
.B text
for its paper and ink, as
.IR rio 's;
.B sketchsel
for what is picked,
.B sketchpoint
for points and constraints,
.B sketchdim
for dimmer marks, and
.B sketchguide
for guides.
.TP
.IR chess (1)
.B chesslight
and
.B chessdark
for the squares,
.B chesssel
for the piece picked and its moves,
.B chesslast
for the last move,
.B chessarrow
for the engine's best move,
.B chesscheck
for a king in check,
.B chesscomment
for comments, and
.B chesserror
for errors;
.BR chesswhite ,
.BR chesswhiteedge ,
.B chessblack
and
.B chessblackedge
fill and edge its pieces, by default
.BR body 's
two colors, each piece edged in the other, and its moves
.BR body 's,
with
.BR tagsel 's
for the move at dot.
.TP
.IR grapw (1)
.B back
and
.B text
for its paper and ink,
.B ltext
for the ring around the point under the mouse, and
.B grapsel
for the points of selected rows.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /lib/theme
the system's theme, night, a dark one
.TP
.B /lib/themes/day
the light theme, Plan 9's own colors; copy it to
.B $home/lib/theme
and start
.I rio
again
